\end{table}

The temporal cohort flags 14.8\% of items as ETS~C, consistent with Li et al.'s 39.5\% total contamination rate---DIF captures only the large-effect-size subset.
The overlap between temporal and quintile flags (Jaccard = 0.58) indicates substantial agreement despite different grouping strategies.

\paragraph{Within-Family Analysis.}
To control for the confound that post-2024 models are both more capable and more contaminated, we perform within-family DIF analysis on Llama (2$\to$3$\to$3.1) and Qwen families.
The 68\% cross-cohort overlap with the full-population DIF flags indicates that most DIF reflects contamination exposure differences rather than pure capability evolution, since within-family capability trajectories are controlled.

\paragraph{Domain Specificity.}
