\subsection{RL Robustness Empirical Validation}

We evaluate DIF detection power across three model cohorts: SFT-only baseline, alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO, $N = 477$), and reasoning-RL (DeepSeek-R1, Qwen2.5-RL, and other GRPO/PPO models mixed into the focal cohort).
Table~\ref{tab:rl_robustness} presents the key comparison.

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{DIF vs.\ baseline detectors across model types. DIF maintains AUROC = 0.91 on reasoning-RL models where ConStat and Min-K\% degrade to near-random.}
\label{tab:rl_robustness}
\small
\begin{tabular}{llcccc}
\toprule
Detector & Cohort & AUROC & 95\% CI & TPR@FPR05 \\
\midrule
DIF (ETS C) & SFT-only & 0.92 & [0.89, 0.95] & 0.79 \\
DIF (ETS C) & Alignment-RL mixed & 0.91 & [0.88, 0.94] & 0.78 \\
