\end{tabular}
\end{table}

DIF retention ratio is 0.97 for alignment-RL and 0.93 for reasoning-RL (TOST equivalence test $p = 0.02$, rejecting the hypothesis that DIF degrades under RL).
The DeLong test confirms the AUROC difference between DIF and ConStat on RL models is statistically significant ($p = 0.0003$).

\paragraph{Partial Exploitation Power Curve.}
Table~\ref{tab:partial_exploit} characterizes detection power as a function of the exploitation rate $p$ (the probability that a model exploits memorized knowledge on a given item).

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{Detection power as a function of exploitation rate $p$. DIF covers $p \geq 0.6$; the ensemble extends coverage to $p \approx 0.4$.}
\label{tab:partial_exploit}
\small
\begin{tabular}{ccccc}
\toprule
$p$ & Effective $\delta$ & ETS C TPR & Ensemble TPR & Coverage Gap \\
\midrule
1.0 & 1.6 & 0.78 & 0.82 & none \\
0.8 & 1.28 & 0.68 & 0.74 & none \\
0.6 & 0.96 & 0.52 & 0.65 & none (ConStat) \\
0.5 & 0.80 & 0.41 & 0.58 & marginal \\
0.4 & 0.64 & 0.30 & 0.48 & ensemble boundary \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

The handoff point between DIF and ensemble coverage occurs at $p \approx 0.52$, where DIF's TPR drops below 0.41 and ConStat's signal (effective for non-RL models) takes over.
Below $p = 0.4$, contamination impact on rankings is minimal ($\delta < 0.64$, corresponding to $<$2 rank positions).

\subsection{Architecture-Stratified DIF}
\label{sec:arch_strat}

IRT's unidimensionality assumption may be violated when the model population includes diverse architectures.
We compare DIF detection on the full population ($N = 5{,}219$) versus a decoder-only subset ($N = 3{,}650$).

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{IRT fit diagnostics by population. Decoder-only subgroup achieves ``good'' fit, full population remains ``acceptable.''}
\label{tab:irt_fit}
\small
\begin{tabular}{lrccccl}
\toprule
Population & $N$ & RMSEA & CFI & TLI & SRMR & Fit Quality \\
\midrule
Full (all architectures) & 5,219 & 0.067 & 0.90 & 0.89 & 0.058 & acceptable \\
Decoder-only & 3,650 & 0.038 & 0.95 & 0.94 & 0.032 & good \\
Decoder-only, neg-disc removed & 3,650 & 0.031 & 0.96 & 0.96 & 0.027 & good \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{DIF detection quality by population. Architecture stratification reduces spurious DIF by 24\%.}
\label{tab:dif_quality_pop}
\small
\begin{tabular}{lccc}
\toprule
Population & TPR ($\delta \geq 1.4$) & FPR & Spurious Reduced \\
\midrule
Full & 0.78 & 0.042 & --- \\
Decoder-only & 0.81 & 0.032 & 125 items \\
\bottomrule
